{"conversation_id":"34cb8bf7-fa09-45a1-b87c-33742b30f7b0","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Root Cause\nIn [`pkg/cache.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/cache.py#L4-L6), `_key(spec)` generated cache keys using `tuple(spec.items())`. In Python dictionaries, iterating over items follows insertion order. As a result, dictionaries with identical keys and values inserted in different orders (such as `{\"region\": \"eu\", \"tier\": \"gold\"}` and `{\"tier\": \"gold\", \"region\": \"eu\"}`) produced different tuple keys, causing lookups with reordered keys to miss the cache and return `None`.\n\nAdditionally, [`pkg/parser.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/parser.py) was missing the implementation of [`parse_duration`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/parser.py#L12-L19), preventing the full test suite from executing.\n\n---\n\n### Fixes Applied\n1. **[`pkg/cache.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/cache.py)**:\n   Updated `_key(spec)` to sort the items deterministically:\n   ```python\n   def _key(spec):\n       return tuple(sorted(spec.items()))\n   ```\n2. **[`pkg/parser.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/parser.py)**:\n   Implemented [`parse_duration`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/pkg/parser.py#L12-L19) to parse compound duration strings (`\"90s\"`, `\"5m\"`, `\"2h30m\"`) and raise `ValueError` on malformed inputs.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\nRan `python -m pytest -v`: All 8 tests passed across [`test_cache.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/test_cache.py), [`test_parser.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/test_parser.py), and [`test_smoke.py`](file:///D:/Projects/subagents-mcp/bench/fixture_repo/test_smoke.py) without modifying any test files.\n","duration_seconds":69.6830558,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":168237,"output_tokens":5280,"thinking_tokens":3091,"cache_read_tokens":267205,"total_tokens":173517}}
